# Safety net. The intended way to publish the design mock-up is:
#
#     bash scripts/build-static-preview.sh
#     npx vercel deploy --prod dist/preview-site
#
# ...which uploads an isolated two-file directory. This file exists for the
# case where someone runs `vercel` in the repository root instead.
#
# It matters because the Vercel CLI uploads the working directory and reads
# THIS file, not .gitignore. The two files holding live API keys are gitignored,
# which means every guard in this repo is blind to them here: check-no-secrets.pl
# skips them by design, the pre-commit hook scans the git index, and CI scans a
# git checkout. None of that protects an upload that never touches git.
#
# A key published this way is public the moment it uploads and must be rotated,
# not deleted.

# Live keys — the reason this file exists
.env
.env.*
preview.html
preview*.html
*.key
*.pem

# WordPress source: PHP served by a static host is delivered as readable text,
# so this would publish the application's source rather than run it.
wp-content/
php/
scripts/
tools/
docs/
design/
.github/
.githooks/
*.zip

# Noise
node_modules/
vendor/
.git/
*.log
